      "content": "Any new respiratory symptoms, even minor shortness of breath or a dry cough, should prompt you to pause and reassess the patient immediately. While mild symptoms might not mandate an instant halt, they are red flags for potential pulmonary toxicity associated with Nitrofurantoin. It is safer to reduce the dose, or potentially switch agents, rather than risk progression to severe pneumonitis. Monitor closely, but do not ignore those early warning signs.",
